<!-- TreatAsLocalProperty: the CI workflow packs each project with a global /p:PackageVersion read
     from that project's own Version property (keep exactly one such tag per csproj; the workflow
     greps for it, so do not spell the tag out in comments). When the sidecar is packed, that global
     value would otherwise leak into this referenced project and the sidecar's nupkg would depend on
     a core version that does not exist (sidecar 0.3.0 on nuget.org depends on core 0.3.0 for exactly
     this reason). Making PackageVersion local pins it to the Version property below, whatever the
     command line says. -->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk" TreatAsLocalProperty="PackageVersion">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0;net11.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <RootNamespace>TechTeaStudio.Injector</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>TechTeaStudio.Injector</AssemblyName>
    <Version>0.5.1</Version>
    <PackageVersion>$(Version)</PackageVersion>

    <Description>Lightweight, expression-tree-compiled dependency injection container for .NET 8/9/10. From-scratch with no Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection dependency. Open generics, decorators, Lazy/Func/Owned auto-resolution, lifecycle hooks (OnActivating / OnActivated), validate-on-build, async disposal, child scopes with extra registrations, modules, assembly scanning, keyed services, and IEnumerable / IReadOnlyDictionary collection injection.</Description>
    <PackageId>TechTeaStudio.Injector</PackageId>
    <PackageTags>di;dependency-injection;ioc;container;injector;open-generics;decorators;lifecycle-hooks;techteastudio</PackageTags>

    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>

    <!-- Turns on both the trimming (IL2xxx) and NativeAOT (IL3xxx) analyzers per-TFM so the
         library's own code is checked. The container is intentionally NOT trim/AOT-safe; the public
         entry points carry [RequiresDynamicCode]/[RequiresUnreferencedCode] so consumers get accurate
         diagnostics, and the analyzers below verify that annotation coverage stays complete. -->
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>

    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/TechTeaStudio/Injector</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>

    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>

    <PackageReleaseNotes>
v0.5.0: Release-blocking engine fixes and keyed-service semantics. First version published to nuget.org after 0.2.0 (0.3.0 and 0.4.0 never shipped because CI failed), so it also carries everything listed under v0.4.0 and v0.3.0.

Added:
  * RegisterDecorator(Type serviceType, Type decoratorType) on IContainerBuilder, so open-generic decorators (IRepository&lt;&gt; -&gt; LoggingRepository&lt;&gt;) are reachable from the public API. An open-generic decorator also wraps closed-only base registrations.
  * ServiceNotRegisteredException.Key; the keyed-miss message now names the key.

Fixed:
  * A singleton whose construction throws is retried on the next resolve instead of replaying the cached exception.
  * Same-thread singleton cycles throw CircularDependencyException (not InvalidOperationException); a cross-thread singleton cycle is detected and reported instead of deadlocking.
  * ResolveKeyed / TryResolveKeyed find keyed open-generic registrations and keyed registrations added to a child scope via BeginLifetimeScope.
  * TryResolve / ResolveOptional of Lazy&lt;T&gt;, Func&lt;T&gt;, Owned&lt;T&gt; answer false / null when T is not registered (Owned&lt;T&gt; used to throw; Lazy/Func used to fail later on use).

Changed:
  * Keyed registrations are no longer the default: Resolve&lt;T&gt;() and IEnumerable&lt;T&gt; / ResolveAll&lt;T&gt;() skip WithKey(...) registrations, and IsRegistered&lt;T&gt;() answers for unkeyed registrations only. Keyed services stay reachable via ResolveKeyed / TryResolveKeyed / ResolveDictionary. This restores Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection keyed-service semantics through the sidecar.

v0.4.0: Engine hardening, faster resolution, and a richer resolution API.

Added:
  * Public keyed resolution: ResolveKeyed&lt;T&gt;(key), ResolveKeyed(Type, key), TryResolveKeyed&lt;T&gt;(key, out value) on IResolver.
  * Non-throwing resolution: TryResolve&lt;T&gt;(out value) and ResolveOptional&lt;T&gt;() (plus Type overloads).
  * Registration probe: IContainer.IsRegistered&lt;T&gt;() / IsRegistered(Type).
  * Open-generic decorators: RegisterDecorator on an open generic now wraps closed resolutions; decorators are pre-indexed by service type.
  * Non-public [Inject] methods are now invoked, matching property injection.

Fixed / changed:
  * Concurrency: _byServiceType is a ConcurrentDictionary, fixing a data race when open generics are closed under concurrent load.
  * Singletons are constructed exactly once under parallel resolution.
  * Lock-free activator caches plus a registration-lookup-before-collection fast path cut per-resolve overhead and lock contention.
  * Func&lt;T&gt; / Lazy&lt;T&gt; / Func&lt;P, T&gt; activators are cached (Func&lt;P, T&gt; no longer recompiles its expression per resolve).

For ASP.NET Core / Generic Host integration use the TechTeaStudio.Injector.Extensions.DependencyInjection sidecar package.

Full changelog: https://github.com/TechTeaStudio/Injector/blob/product/CHANGELOG.md
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\icon.png"     Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\README.md"    Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\CHANGELOG.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE.txt"  Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
